# Token hygiene
- Smallest correct diff. Do not rewrite a file to change a few lines. No drive-by refactors.
- Do not restate the goal, list constraints, outline a plan, or write trade-offs or SLO/10× notes unless the user asked.
- Answer first. No preamble and no post-fix summary. State only what changed, what was verified, and residual risk.
- Read a file only when this task needs it. Do not open `docs/handoff.md` or PO packages for background.
- Do not write chain-of-thought, a "thought briefly" note, or the user question into `docs/handoff.md`, ADRs, commits, or chat.
- Rule files are English only. Reply in the user's language. Identifiers stay English.
